        <div class="drivers-panels setup-panels popup-scroll">
          <section class="drivers-panel setup-panel" data-drivers-tab="list">
            <p class="panel-hint" id="drivers-list-hint">Each driver card shows its connection summary. Edit a driver for type-specific settings. Device templates add tags onto a driver below.</p>
            <div class="toolbar wrap">
              <button type="button" id="btn-hw-wizard" class="btn primary">Hardware wizard…</button>
              <span class="muted">Guided setup — same as <strong>Apply device template</strong> below</span>
            </div>
            <details class="device-template-bar">
              <summary>Apply device template (optional)</summary>
              <p class="panel-hint">Adds I/O tags from a template onto a driver (no server restart). <strong>Modbus:</strong> edit a driver for COM port; each apply uses the <strong>next slave address</strong>. <strong>HAL</strong> (e.g. Sequent SM-I-001): applies <code>hal</code> driver + plugin path + <code>stack</code> / I2C bus — edit those in the driver row after apply.</p>
              <div class="toolbar wrap">
                <label>Template
                  <select id="device-preset"></select>
                </label>
                <label id="device-concube-groups-wrap" class="device-concube-opt view-hidden">Parameter groups (×4)
                  <input type="number" id="device-concube-groups" min="1" max="16" value="1" title="Each group adds 4 parameters (PARMn_STS + PARMn_VAL). Apply again to append the next group.">
                </label>
                <button type="button" id="btn-device-apply" class="btn primary">Apply template</button>
                <label class="device-template-replace">
                  <input type="checkbox" id="device-template-replace"> Replace tags on this driver
                </label>
                <span id="device-apply-msg" class="muted"></span>
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="device-template-bar">
              <summary>Add Opta Parc devices (bulk)</summary>
              <p class="panel-hint">Each driver has a permanent <strong>position ID</strong> (plant name) and a physical <strong>device ID</strong> (<code>opta_</code> + serial). Tags and ST bind to position — use <strong>Replace hardware</strong> when an Opta is swapped.</p>
              <div class="form-grid compact">
                <label class="span-all">Position ID (permanent)
                  <input id="parc-opta-position-id" placeholder="motor_skid_main" title="Optional when adding one device — auto-suggested from registry if blank">
                </label>
                <label class="span-all">Physical device ID
                  <input id="parc-opta-single-id" placeholder="opta_012355b52d66a109ee" title="One Opta — ATECC SN-based id from firmware, or legacy opta_st_01">
                </label>
                <label class="span-all">Or multiple IDs (one per line)
                  <textarea id="parc-opta-bulk-ids" rows="3" placeholder="opta_st_02&#10;opta_st_03"></textarea>
                </label>
                <label class="checkbox-inline span-all">
                  <input type="checkbox" id="parc-opta-bulk-use-range"> Use numeric range (bulk)
                </label>
                <label id="parc-opta-range-prefix-wrap">Prefix <input id="parc-opta-bulk-prefix" value="opta_st_"></label>
                <label id="parc-opta-range-start-wrap">Start <input id="parc-opta-bulk-start" type="number" value="1" min="0"></label>
                <label id="parc-opta-range-count-wrap">Count <input id="parc-opta-bulk-count" type="number" value="1" min="1"></label>
                <label id="parc-opta-range-pad-wrap">Pad <input id="parc-opta-bulk-pad" type="number" value="2" min="0" title="Zero-pad numeric suffix"></label>
              </div>
              <div class="toolbar wrap">
                <label class="checkbox-inline"><input type="checkbox" id="parc-opta-bulk-from-registry" checked> Add from Parc registry (MQTT devices — ATECC serial ids)</label>
                <label class="checkbox-inline view-hidden" id="parc-opta-noise-wrap"><input type="checkbox" id="parc-opta-bulk-include-noise"> Include test/debug IDs (test-*, dbg-*, …)</label>
                <label class="checkbox-inline"><input type="checkbox" id="parc-opta-bulk-sync" checked> Sync tags after add</label>
                <button type="button" id="btn-parc-opta-bulk" class="btn primary">Add Opta Parc drivers</button>
                <span id="parc-opta-bulk-msg" class="muted"></span>
              </div>
              <div id="parc-registry-device-list" class="parc-registry-list panel-hint"></div>
            </details>
            <div class="toolbar">
              <button type="button" id="btn-drv-add" class="btn">Add driver</button>
              <button type="button" id="btn-drv-refresh-ports" class="btn">Refresh ports</button>
              <button type="button" id="btn-drv-save" class="btn primary">Save drivers</button>
            </div>
            <p id="drivers-test-status" class="muted cell-mono" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <div id="drivers-panel" class="popup-scroll"></div>
          </section>
          <section class="drivers-panel setup-panel view-hidden" data-drivers-tab="modbus">
            <p class="panel-hint">One-shot register block copy between Modbus RTU (USB/serial) and Modbus TCP — useful for commissioning and migration.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>RTU port
                <select id="peaklogic-rtu-port"></select>
              </label>
              <label>Baud <input id="peaklogic-rtu-baud" type="number" value="9600"></label>
              <label>RTU slave <input id="peaklogic-rtu-slave" type="number" value="1"></label>
              <label>TCP host <input id="peaklogic-tcp-host" value="127.0.0.1"></label>
              <label>TCP port <input id="peaklogic-tcp-port" type="number" value="502"></label>
              <label>RTU addr <input id="peaklogic-rtu-addr" type="number" value="0"></label>
              <label>TCP addr <input id="peaklogic-tcp-addr" type="number" value="0"></label>
              <label>Count <input id="peaklogic-count" type="number" value="10"></label>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar">
              <button type="button" id="peaklogic-rtu-tcp" class="btn primary">Move RTU → TCP</button>
              <button type="button" id="peaklogic-tcp-rtu" class="btn">Move TCP → RTU</button>
            </div>
            <pre id="peaklogic-result" class="log"></pre>
          </section>
          <section class="drivers-panel setup-panel view-hidden" data-drivers-tab="nextcentury">
            <p class="panel-hint">Cloud API polling for NextCentury Meters — <strong>not</strong> Modbus or a COM port. On each poll the driver can <strong>auto-create tags</strong> from report rows (deviceId + usage/temp/leak). Use <strong>Fill from example</strong> for credentials; <strong>Load example tags</strong> is optional when auto-sync is off.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>Driver ID <input id="nc-driver-id" value="nextcentury1" autocomplete="off"></label>
              <label>Email <input id="nc-email" type="email" autocomplete="username" placeholder="user@example.com"></label>
              <label>Password <input id="nc-password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password"></label>
              <label>Report ID <input id="nc-report-id" value="rt_4510"></label>
              <label>Poll interval ms <input id="nc-poll-ms" type="number" min="60000" step="1000" value="900000" title="Default 900000 = 15 minutes"></label>
              <label>Devices per site (plan) <input id="nc-devices-per-site" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1500" title="Planning estimate — devices per NextCentury property/site"></label>
              <label>Property IDs <input id="nc-property-ids" placeholder="39990, 40074 (blank = all)"></label>
              <label class="checkbox-inline"><input type="checkbox" id="nc-auto-sync-tags" checked> Auto-sync tags on each poll</label>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar wrap">
              <button type="button" id="nc-fill-example" class="btn">Fill from example</button>
              <button type="button" id="nc-test" class="btn">Test connection</button>
              <button type="button" id="nc-open-portal" class="btn" title="Sign in to app.nextcenturymeters.com with the credentials above">Open portal</button>
              <button type="button" id="nc-save-connect" class="btn primary">Save &amp; connect</button>
              <button type="button" id="nc-load-example-tags" class="btn" title="Merge tags from st/fixtures/tags.nextcentury.json">Load example tags</button>
            </div>
            <p id="nc-deploy-estimate" class="prog-deploy-estimate muted cell-mono" aria-live="polite" title="Estimated tag count and scan load per poll"></p>
            <p id="nc-status" class="muted cell-mono" aria-live="polite"></p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

