        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-help-context" data-help-section="historian-logger" title="Help: Logger config">Help</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn popup-close" data-popup-close="historian-logger" title="Close">Close</button>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="popup-body historian-logger-body popup-scroll">
      <p class="panel-hint">MongoDB archive, which tags are logged (<strong>Hist</strong>), runtime auto-start, and PdM asset maps. Trend chart pens are under <strong>Pen config…</strong>.</p>

      <h3 class="setup-subhead">MongoDB connection</h3>
      <p id="hist-log-mongo-status" class="logging-status cell-mono muted">MongoDB logger: checking…</p>
      <div class="form-grid compact">
        <label>MongoDB URI
          <input id="hist-log-uri" value="mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017" placeholder="mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017" autocomplete="off">
        </label>
        <label>Database
          <input id="hist-log-db" value="peaklogic" placeholder="peaklogic">
        </label>
        <label>SCADA collection
          <input id="hist-log-collection" value="tag_logs" placeholder="tag_logs">
        </label>
        <label>Edge AI collection
          <input id="hist-log-edge-collection" value="edge_inference" placeholder="edge_inference">
        </label>
        <label>Sample interval (ms)
          <input id="hist-log-sample-ms" type="number" min="1000" value="5000">
        </label>
        <label class="historian-ctl">
          <input type="checkbox" id="hist-log-auto-start" checked> Auto-start runtime on boot (driver polling + logging)
        </label>
      </div>

      <h3 class="setup-subhead">Tags logged to MongoDB (Hist)</h3>
      <p class="panel-hint">Checked tags are written to <code>pen_sample</code> while the runtime runs. Same as the <strong>Hist</strong> column in <strong>Tags</strong>.</p>
      <div id="hist-log-tags-wrap" class="hist-log-tags-wrap table-wrap"></div>

      <h3 class="setup-subhead">PdM assets</h3>
      <p class="panel-hint">Asset → SCADA tag maps for <strong>Historian → PdM (SCADA + Edge)</strong> source. Also editable as JSON under <strong>System setup → PdM</strong>.</p>
      <div class="pdm-asset-editor form-grid compact">
        <label>Asset ID
          <input type="text" id="historian-pdm-asset-id" placeholder="pump-101" autocomplete="off">
        </label>
        <label>SCADA tags <span class="muted">(Ctrl+click multi-select)</span>
          <select id="historian-pdm-asset-tag-pick" multiple size="6"></select>
        </label>
        <div class="toolbar wrap pdm-asset-actions">
          <button type="button" id="btn-historian-pdm-asset-save" class="btn">Save asset</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-historian-pdm-asset-new" class="btn">New</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-historian-pdm-asset-delete" class="btn">Delete</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pdm-asset-table-wrap">
        <table class="data-table compact" id="historian-pdm-asset-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Asset</th><th>SCADA tags</th><th></th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="historian-pdm-asset-tbody"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p id="historian-pdm-asset-msg" class="muted cell-mono"></p>
      <p id="hist-log-save-msg" class="muted cell-mono"></p>
    </div>
    <footer class="popup-footer">
      <button type="button" id="btn-hist-log-save" class="btn primary">Save logger settings</button>
    </footer>
    <div class="popup-resize-handle popup-resize-w" data-resize="w" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="popup-resize-handle popup-resize-s" data-resize="s" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="popup-resize-handle popup-resize-e" data-resize="e" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="popup-resize-handle popup-resize-sw" data-resize="sw" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="popup-resize-handle popup-resize-se" data-resize="se" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- Historian report popup -->
  <div class="app-popup view-hidden" data-popup="report" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="popup-report-title">
    <div class="popup-chrome popup-chrome-report">
      <header class="popup-header popup-header-split">
        <h2 id="popup-report-title">Historian report</h2>
        <div class="popup-header-actions">
          <button type="button" class="btn popup-close" data-popup-close="report" title="Close">Close</button>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="popup-body popup-scroll">
        <p class="panel-hint">Export or print historian data from the live buffer or MongoDB archive. Configure pens via <strong>Historian → Pen config…</strong>; MongoDB and Hist tags via <strong>Logger config…</strong>.</p>
        <div class="toolbar wrap historian-toolbar">
          <label class="historian-ctl">Source
            <select id="report-source">
              <option value="live">Live buffer</option>
              <option value="mongo">MongoDB archive</option>
              <option value="pdm">PdM (SCADA + Edge)</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="historian-ctl">Range
            <select id="report-range">
              <option value="1h">Last 1 hour</option>
              <option value="6h">Last 6 hours</option>
              <option value="12h">Last 12 hours</option>
              <option value="24h" selected>Last 24 hours</option>
              <option value="7d">Last 7 days</option>
              <option value="30d">Last 30 days</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="historian-ctl historian-custom-dates">
            <input type="checkbox" id="report-use-custom"> Custom
          </label>
          <label class="historian-ctl historian-date-ctl">From
            <input type="datetime-local" id="report-from" class="historian-datetime">
          </label>
          <label class="historian-ctl historian-date-ctl">To
            <input type="datetime-local" id="report-to" class="historian-datetime">
          </label>
          <label class="historian-ctl report-pdm-only view-hidden">Asset
            <select id="report-pdm-asset"></select>
          </label>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-load-mongo" class="btn">Load archive</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-load-pdm" class="btn report-pdm-only view-hidden">Load PdM</button>
          <span id="report-load-msg" class="muted"></span>
          <span id="report-pdm-summary" class="muted report-pdm-only view-hidden"></span>
        </div>
        <div id="report-pdm-forecast" class="pdm-forecast-banner report-pdm-only view-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <p id="report-meta" class="muted cell-mono"></p>
        <canvas id="report-chart-canvas" class="report-chart-preview" width="1100" height="280"></canvas>
        <div id="report-pen-table" class="table-wrap report-pen-table"></div>
        <details class="report-config-panel" id="report-config-panel">
          <summary>PDF layout &amp; sections</summary>
          <div class="form-grid compact report-config-grid">
            <label>Title <input type="text" id="report-cfg-title" maxlength="120"></label>
            <label>Subtitle <input type="text" id="report-cfg-subtitle" maxlength="200"></label>
            <label>Company <input type="text" id="report-cfg-company" maxlength="120"></label>
            <label>Footer <input type="text" id="report-cfg-footer" maxlength="200"></label>
            <label>Page
              <select id="report-cfg-page-size">
                <option value="A4">A4</option>
                <option value="LETTER">Letter</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Orientation
              <select id="report-cfg-orientation">
                <option value="landscape">Landscape</option>
                <option value="portrait">Portrait</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Chart height (pt) <input type="number" id="report-cfg-chart-h" min="80" max="400" value="220"></label>
          </div>
          <div class="report-config-sections">
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-cover" checked> Cover / header</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-chart" checked> Trend chart</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-pen-table" checked> Pen summary table</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-statistics" checked> Statistics</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-forecast" checked> Failure forecast</label>
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="report-sec-notes" checked> Notes</label>
          </div>
          <label class="report-config-notes">Notes
            <textarea id="report-cfg-notes" rows="3" maxlength="4000" placeholder="Optional remarks for the PDF report"></textarea>
          </label>
          <div class="toolbar wrap">
            <button type="button" id="btn-report-save-config" class="btn">Save layout</button>
            <span id="report-config-msg" class="muted"></span>
          </div>
        </details>
        <div class="toolbar wrap">
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-download-pdf" class="btn primary">Download PDF</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-export-csv" class="btn">Export CSV</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-export-pdm-csv" class="btn report-pdm-only view-hidden">Export PdM CSV</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-print-pdf" class="btn">Print preview</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-report-open-setup" class="btn">Pen config…</button>
          <span id="report-export-msg" class="muted"></span>
        </div>
        <details class="report-mongo-logs-panel" id="report-mongo-logs-panel">
          <summary>MongoDB logs (system, hardware, historian)</summary>
          <p class="panel-hint">Operational logs stored in MongoDB or local fallback files — hardware change-outs, system errors, and tag historian status.</p>
          <div class="report-mongo-tabs toolbar wrap" role="tablist" aria-label="Mongo log sections">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm report-mongo-tab active" data-report-mongo-tab="syslog" role="tab" aria-selected="true">System log</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm report-mongo-tab" data-report-mongo-tab="hardware" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Hardware history</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm report-mongo-tab" data-report-mongo-tab="historian" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Historian / tags</button>
          </div>
          <div class="toolbar wrap report-mongo-toolbar">
            <label class="report-mongo-filter report-mongo-syslog-only">Level
              <select id="report-mongo-syslog-level">
                <option value="">All</option>
                <option value="error">Error</option>
                <option value="warn">Warn</option>
                <option value="info">Info</option>
                <option value="maintenance">Maintenance</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label class="report-mongo-filter report-mongo-syslog-only">Category
              <input type="text" id="report-mongo-syslog-category" placeholder="e.g. hardware" maxlength="64">
            </label>
            <label>Limit
              <input type="number" id="report-mongo-limit" min="10" max="500" value="100" class="report-mongo-limit-input">
            </label>
            <button type="button" id="btn-report-mongo-refresh" class="btn btn-sm">Refresh</button>
            <button type="button" id="btn-report-mongo-open-historian" class="btn btn-sm report-mongo-historian-only view-hidden">Open Historian</button>
            <span id="report-mongo-msg" class="muted"></span>
          </div>
          <p id="report-mongo-status" class="muted cell-mono report-mongo-status-line"></p>
          <div id="report-mongo-syslog" class="table-wrap report-mongo-table report-mongo-pane" data-report-mongo-pane="syslog" role="tabpanel">
            <p class="muted">Open this panel or click Refresh to load system log entries.</p>
          </div>
          <div id="report-mongo-hardware" class="table-wrap report-mongo-table report-mongo-pane view-hidden" data-report-mongo-pane="hardware" role="tabpanel">
            <p class="muted">Click Refresh to load hardware change-out history.</p>
          </div>
          <div id="report-mongo-historian" class="report-mongo-pane view-hidden" data-report-mongo-pane="historian" role="tabpanel">
            <p class="muted">Click Refresh to load tag historian status.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Unified Setup popup -->
  <div class="app-popup view-hidden" data-popup="project" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="popup-project-title">
    <div class="popup-chrome popup-chrome-wide popup-chrome-setup">
      <header class="popup-header popup-header-split">
        <h2 id="popup-project-title">System setup</h2>
        <div class="popup-header-actions">
          <button type="button" id="btn-setup-context-help" class="btn btn-sm btn-help-context" data-help-section="system-setup" title="Help: System setup">Help</button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-proj-apply-header" class="btn primary">Apply all</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn popup-close" data-popup-close="project" title="Close">Close</button>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="setup-shell">
        <nav class="setup-nav" aria-label="Setup sections">
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab active" data-setup-tab-btn="general">General</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="features">Features</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="hardware">Hardware</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="logging">Logging</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="pdm">PdM</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="roi">ROI</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="hmi">HMI</button>
          <button type="button" class="setup-tab" data-setup-tab-btn="projects">Projects</button>
        </nav>
        <div class="setup-panels popup-scroll">

          <section class="setup-panel" data-setup-tab="general">
            <p class="panel-hint">Project identity and scan rate. Map tags to drivers in <strong>Tags</strong> / <strong>Drivers</strong>.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>Project name
                <input id="proj-name" placeholder="e.g. line_a" value="">
              </label>
              <label>Active ST program
                <select id="proj-active-program"></select>
              </label>
              <label>Scan interval (ms)
                <input id="proj-scan-ms" type="number" min="10" max="10000" value="100">
              </label>
              <label>Starting HMI screen
                <select id="proj-hmi-home-screen"></select>
              </label>
            </div>
            <p class="panel-hint">The selected screen loads first on the main HMI page. Use the navigation bar to switch screens after load. Configure screens, layout, and bindings in the <strong>HMI</strong> tab or via <strong>Setup…</strong> on the HMI panel.</p>
            <h3 class="setup-subhead">On startup</h3>
            <p class="panel-hint">Applied when PeakLogic boots (before drivers connect). Alarm notification users are under <strong>Alarms → Notification users…</strong>.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>Load on boot
                <select id="proj-startup-mode">
                  <option value="workspace">Last workspace (<code>workspace.est.json</code>)</option>
                  <option value="last_project">Last opened saved project</option>
                  <option value="saved_project">Specific saved project</option>
                  <option value="blank">Current data folder only (no .est load)</option>
                </select>
              </label>
              <label id="proj-startup-project-wrap">Startup project
                <select id="proj-startup-project"></select>
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-startup-prompt"> Show reminder if startup load fails
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-auto-start-runtime"> Auto-start runtime on boot (Program → Start)
              </label>
            </div>
            <h3 class="setup-subhead">MQTT Parc (Opta)</h3>
            <p class="panel-hint">Central MQTT hub for all Opta Parc devices. Enable before bulk-adding drivers or when Optas report to the broker. Broker URL is shared by every <code>mqtt_parc</code> driver.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-mqtt-parc-enabled"> Enable MQTT Parc hub
              </label>
              <label>Broker URL
                <input id="proj-mqtt-parc-broker" placeholder="mqtt://192.168.1.233:1883" title="Mosquitto or LAN MQTT broker">
              </label>
              <label class="span-all">Global site key (hex, e.g. 0x0001)
                <input id="proj-mqtt-parc-global-site-key" placeholder="0x0001" spellcheck="false">
                <span class="muted">Must match Opta /setup Global site key; topics <code>peaklogic/v1/g/{key}/{tag}</code>.</span>
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-remote-execution"> Remote ST execution (run logic on Opta via MQTT)
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-opta-autorun"> Auto-run ST on Opta after power-up (requires NV program + deploy once)
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-mqtt-parc-auto-discover"> Auto-discover Opta drivers from MQTT reports
              </label>
            </div>
            <h3 class="setup-subhead">Cloud remote (appliance uplink)</h3>
            <p class="panel-hint">When this PeakLogic runs as a site appliance, relay Parc telemetry to a cloud VM tenant topic <code>peaklogic/v1/{tenantId}/{deviceId}/telemetry</code>. Set the same <code>tenantId</code> on the cloud VM and use the appliance <code>gatewayId</code> from pairing.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-cloud-remote-enabled"> Enable cloud remote uplink
              </label>
              <label>Tenant ID
                <input id="proj-cloud-tenant-id" placeholder="acme-corp" spellcheck="false">
              </label>
              <label>Gateway ID (appliance UUID)
                <input id="proj-cloud-gateway-id" placeholder="uuid-from-pairing" spellcheck="false">
              </label>
              <label class="span-all">Cloud broker URL
                <input id="proj-cloud-broker-url" placeholder="mqtt://&lt;droplet-ip&gt;:1883">
              </label>
            </div>
            <p class="panel-hint">Optional cloud tools (virtual devices, cellular SIM inventory): open the <button type="button" class="btn-link setup-tab-jump" data-setup-tab-btn="features">Features</button> tab.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="setup-panel view-hidden" data-setup-tab="features">
            <p class="panel-hint">Enable optional cloud tools on this PC appliance. Check a box, click <strong>Apply all settings</strong>, then reload the page so <strong>Open</strong> links appear below. No <code>.env</code> changes required.</p>
            <h3 class="setup-subhead">Cloud Sim management</h3>
            <p class="panel-hint">Create virtual Opta / Modbus devices that publish tenant-scoped MQTT telemetry.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-cloud-sims-enabled"> Enable Cloud Sim management
              </label>
            </div>
            <% if (cloudSimsEnabled) { %>
            <div class="toolbar wrap">
              <a href="/cloud/sims" class="btn primary" data-cloud-sims-open>Open Cloud Sims</a>
            </div>
            <% } %>
            <h3 class="setup-subhead">Cellular SIM management</h3>
            <p class="panel-hint">Track IoT SIM/eSIM inventory from Hologram, Twilio, and other vendors.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label class="historian-ctl span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-cellular-sims-enabled"> Enable Cellular SIM management
              </label>
            </div>
            <% if (cellularSimsEnabled) { %>
            <div class="toolbar wrap">
              <a href="/cellular/sims" class="btn primary" data-cellular-sims-open>Open Cellular SIMs</a>
            </div>
            <% } %>
          </section>

          <section class="setup-panel view-hidden" data-setup-tab="hardware">
            <p class="panel-hint">Defaults for new RTU drivers and the default device template.</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>Default serial port
                <select id="proj-default-port"></select>
              </label>
              <label>Default baud
                <input id="proj-default-baud" type="number" value="9600">
              </label>
              <label>Default slave ID
                <input id="proj-default-slave" type="number" min="1" max="255" value="1">
              </label>
              <label>Default device template
                <select id="proj-default-preset"></select>
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar wrap">
              <button type="button" id="btn-proj-apply-template" class="btn">Apply default device template</button>
            </div>
            <div class="logging-block" id="proj-alf-mech-wrap">
              <h3 class="setup-subhead">Assisted living — mechanical room</h3>
              <p class="panel-hint">Domestic hot water: one flow meter feeds three 120 gal heaters. Choose electric (kW meters) or gas (gas flow meter).</p>
              <label class="checkbox-inline span-all">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-alf-mech-wh-gas"> Gas-fired water heaters (show gas flow meter). Unchecked = electric (power meters).
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="logging-block" id="proj-alf-pools-wrap">
              <h3 class="setup-subhead">Site — bodies of water &amp; sanitation</h3>
              <p class="panel-hint">Up to <strong>4 bodies of water</strong> (pools, spas, water features) and <strong>8 filter pumps</strong> site-wide (max 2 per body). Set body type (main pool, spa, or water feature), which main pool shared plumbing connects to, filter pump count, and daily circulation targets here. Spas and water features share water with a main pool but keep their own flow rates (e.g. pool 6–8 h/day, spa 0.5 h/day). Edit weekly run schedules on the pool HMI → <strong>Schedules</strong> screen.</p>
              <div id="proj-alf-pools-list" class="proj-alf-pools-list"></div>
              <p id="proj-alf-site-pump-total" class="panel-hint muted">Site filter pumps: 1 / 8</p>
              <div class="toolbar wrap">
                <button type="button" id="btn-proj-alf-pool-add" class="btn btn-sm">Add body of water</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="setup-panel view-hidden" data-setup-tab="logging">
            <p class="panel-hint">MongoDB connection, <strong>Hist</strong> tags, runtime auto-start, and PdM assets: <strong>Historian → Logger config…</strong>. Use this tab for archive maintenance.</p>

            <div class="logging-block logging-tools">
              <h3 class="setup-subhead">Archive tools</h3>
              <div class="logging-tool-grid">
                <div class="logging-tool-card">
                  <h4>Demo seed</h4>
                  <p class="panel-hint">Insert <strong>90 days</strong> of random samples: <strong>4 digital</strong> (<code>SEED_DI1</code>–4) and <strong>6 analog</strong> (<code>SEED_AI1</code>–6) at 15 min intervals. Adds tags and historian pens.</p>
                  <div class="toolbar wrap">
                    <button type="button" id="btn-mongo-seed" class="btn">Seed 90-day demo data</button>
                    <span id="mongo-seed-msg" class="muted"></span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="logging-tool-card logging-tool-card-danger">
                  <h4>Purge archive</h4>
                  <p class="panel-hint">Delete <code>pen_sample</code> and <code>pen_selection</code> documents. Does not clear the in-memory historian buffer.</p>
                  <div class="toolbar wrap historian-toolbar">
                    <label class="historian-ctl">From
                      <input type="datetime-local" id="purge-from" class="historian-datetime">
                    </label>
                    <label class="historian-ctl">To
                      <input type="datetime-local" id="purge-to" class="historian-datetime">
                    </label>
                    <button type="button" id="btn-mongo-purge" class="btn">Purge range</button>
                    <button type="button" id="btn-mongo-purge-all" class="btn btn-danger">Purge all</button>
                    <span id="mongo-purge-msg" class="muted"></span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="setup-panel view-hidden" data-setup-tab="pdm">
            <p class="panel-hint">Predictive maintenance: map SCADA historian tags to assets, align with edge AI inference, and build feature windows in MongoDB. View combined trends under <strong>Historian → PdM (SCADA + Edge)</strong>.</p>
            <p id="pdm-batch-status" class="logging-status cell-mono muted">PdM batch: checking…</p>
            <div class="form-grid compact">
              <label>Window size (minutes)
                <input id="proj-pdm-window-min" type="number" min="1" max="60" value="5">
              </label>
              <label>Health failure threshold (0–1)
                <input id="proj-pdm-failure-threshold" type="number" min="0.05" max="0.95" step="0.05" value="0.3">
              </label>
              <label>Features collection
                <input id="proj-pdm-features-collection" value="pdm_features" placeholder="pdm_features">
              </label>
              <label class="historian-ctl">
                <input type="checkbox" id="proj-pdm-build-enabled"> Nightly feature batch
              </label>
